    interp_result_question_operator_wrapper_unmatchable_2026-09-01, 1, "2026-11-09 (work/p3-subj4-seed-20261109) status open->documented: root cause is lexical, not a `?` lowering defect — `f()?.m()` lexes as the SAFE-NAVIGATION operator `?.` (Err/None -> nil), so a Result wrapper written that way returns nil, matching neither Ok nor Err at the caller. The try-then-call form `(f()?).m()` unwraps Ok and early-returns Err. Pinned by test/01_unit/compiler/95.interp/interpreter/result_try_receiver_prevention_spec.spl (a0486f1b7e8, in release/1.0.0): seed binary runs it 4/4 GREEN under SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpreter. Verified both shapes on the seed: unparenthesised falls through match arms (nil), parenthesised classifies correctly."

